            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at 7 Bridges Craft Beer Taproom & Restaurant / Đông Du",
            "review_text": "Mark D\nCampbell, California\n108 contributions\n0\nMy first and last beer in Vietnam\nSep 2026 • Couples\n7 Bridges Craft Beer Taproom & Restaurant on Đông Du was my home away from home during my stay. It was where I had my first beer in Vietnam, and it's where I'll have my last one on this trip. It's a taproom and restaurant in one, so you can come for a drink, stay for a meal, or do both. I believe the taproom is open late, which makes it a great spot for a nightcap after a long day of exploring.\n\nMy first beer here was the Heritage Superdry, and it turned out to be an award winner. It took Champion Beer of Asia at the 2025 Asia Beer Championship, chosen from 812 entries. It's a rice lager brewed with Vietnamese broken rice, an ingredient with a special place in Vietnamese cooking. The result is a light body, clean flavor, and a crisp, refreshing finish. Rather than going for heavy or complex, it's all about subtlety and balance, which makes it easy to drink in Saigon's heat. 7 Bridges brews it in-house, and it's on draft at all of their taprooms across Vietnam.\n\nThe beer selection is huge, with 40 beers on tap, including guest beers. If you enjoy craft beer, it's a great chance to try something different from the standard local lagers.\n\nThe food is just as good. When I was moving between hotels, this was where we went for pizza. We tried the pepperoni and the fancy mushroom pizza, and both were so yummy. They also make their own chilli sauce, which is worth adding to your slices.\n\nIt's an easy place to settle in, whether you're catching up with friends or cooling off after a day of sightseeing. I'd happily come back, and I'm even planning to pick up one of their t-shirts to take home.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 28, 2026",
